1. runc is the low level process that setup namespaces, cgroup for containers

2. there are three things here, containerd, shim-runc, runc. we talk to containerd via
docker, nerdctl etc and then containerd starts the shim-runc(small helper process), which
then talks with runc to create the container. Right now runc is parent process of the 
container, but to make container running independent of runc, shim-runc become its parent and
runc exits and then shim-runc handels the containers

3. each container has its own parent shim-runc process.

nerdctl/docker --> containerd ---> shim-runc ---> runc(it create container(cgroup,namespace)).

4. Buildkit is use to build the docker image, it parses the Dockerfile, plan the steps, 
cache results, creates the layers, and assemble the final image.

Builkit take help of runc or containerd, to creates the image layers, here, for every RUN command in the dockerfile, a tempory container run and inside that container that RUN
command runs and then temporary container gets stop and filesystem changes get saved in the docker image layers

so this temporary container is created by runc

so flow is like this:

buildkit --> runc
OR
buildkit ---> containerd ---> shim-runc ---> runc

which buildkit use runc directly or via containerd depends on which worker is enabled in buildkit.

5. buildkitctl is use to interact with buildkit.